From: "Baptiste G." <70719480+BeeeFX@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:32:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Properties panels: name the header for stylesheets

The header of a properties panel (name field, colour, undo/redo, float, close...) is a plain QFrame, so a
stylesheet couldn't tell its buttons from the knobs' own buttons below. It is now named
"DockablePanelHeader" (QFrame#DockablePanelHeader QPushButton { ... }). Nothing else changes.

Core patch 0002 of the BeeeFX fork (layer/patches/), written to be offered upstream as it is.

Gap: layer/GAPS.md, "Nuke's look and habits" (the properties panels' header buttons).
Size: 1 file, 2 lines added.
upstream: not offered yet (to offer to Niik-l: github.com/Niik-l/Natron).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Gui/DockablePanel.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Gui/DockablePanel.cpp b/Gui/DockablePanel.cpp
index 51d9f813..573aba38 100644
--- a/Gui/DockablePanel.cpp
+++ b/Gui/DockablePanel.cpp
@@ -185,6 +185,8 @@ DockablePanel::DockablePanel(Gui* gui,
     if (headerMode != eHeaderModeNoHeader) {
         _imp->_headerWidget = new QFrame(this);
         _imp->_headerWidget->setFrameShape(QFrame::Box);
+        // A name the stylesheet can aim at: the header's buttons, apart from the knobs' own buttons.
+        _imp->_headerWidget->setObjectName( QString::fromUtf8("DockablePanelHeader") );
         _imp->_headerLayout = new QHBoxLayout(_imp->_headerWidget);
         _imp->_headerLayout->setContentsMargins(0, 0, 0, 0);
         _imp->_headerWidget->setSizePolicy(QSizePolicy::Preferred, QSizePolicy::Fixed);
